  "placementWhy": "Good (about 5 m): scale from the 600 ft bar (819 px, 0.2233 m/px; its metre bar agrees); turned 1.94 degrees from the N mag arrow (2003) so the Tulum - Coba road the map draws along the cave's south-west side (two dashed edges 9.6 m apart, read by hand along their whole length) runs parallel to the real highway (the satellite's asphalt, fitted as a line), then put on it: the database's Cenote Vaca Ha (Google) at the entrance - the passage's south-east end - moved 14 m north-east; the map's road centreline then lies on the highway's along its whole length (within 0.3 degrees and 3 m). Checked on the satellite too: the map's road to Cenote Tortaga lies on the track running north-east, its access road on the path from the highway to the entrance. The coordinates printed on the map (20 16.245 N, 87 28.892 W) are about 100 m west of this: placed there, the cave straddled the highway.",
